Test conservation, ownership, uniqueness, monotonicity, quorum, finality, epoch/height/time, snapshot, cache, and atomicity assumptions. Look for inconsistent state views between components, partial writes, rollback gaps, rounding and precision drift, signed/unsigned conversion, duplicated credit, missing debit, stale derived state, race and interleaving windows, reorg or retry behavior, proposer/validator asymmetry, nondeterministic iteration, and validation performed against a different representation or state version than execution. Build the shortest adversarial sequence that crosses the relevant components.

Emit every distinct code-grounded technical vulnerability before bounty scope, severity, deduplication, or reproduction gates. Set exploitable=true only when the least-privileged actor and end-to-end trigger are established. If the faulty operation is concrete but one material deployment, dependency, or reachability fact remains open, set exploitable=false and preserve it with the exact evidence gap in explanation. Never invent unavailable source behavior. Return a stub only when no concrete vulnerable operation exists under this lens. Point file_path and line to the root faulty operation and make trigger_flow an ordered path:line:symbol sequence.
